Yes, the shaded region is the union of two quarter-circles of radius $2\sqrt{2}$ minus the rectangle inside the quarter-circles. The radius of each circle is half the diameter. The area of each is 
\[ \frac{1}{4}\pi r^2 = 2\pi \]
and the area of the rectangle is
\[ r^2 = 8 \]
so the total area is
\[ 2(2\pi) - 8 = 4\pi - 8 = \boxed{8 - 4\sqrt{2}} \times \pi. \]

